d out.<br /> <br /> Glad to see things are finally moving!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-04T23:05:53-08:00","id":1531998,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/curseborne/1512116-curseborne?p=1531989#post1531989\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Your circles are not mine. We're having a great time seeing the document previews and collating them on the Discord.</div> </div> </div> </div>Was Cruseborne Preview publicly available somewhere? Or is everything closed to the Onyx Path Discord? (Which I don't have to access <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Was banned last year there for asking about books premiers times. )","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude1e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-05T06:26:55-08:00","id":1532011,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/curseborne/1512116-curseborne?p=1531998#post1531998\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Was Cruseborne Preview publicly available somewhere? Or is everything closed to the Onyx Path Discord? (Which I don't have to access <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Was banned last year there for asking about books premiers times. )</div> </div> </div> </div>There's some stuff provided to Dork Tales and similar RPG community influencers as a deliberate leak:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://twitter.com/VeeIsForVampire/status/1764623237244170421\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://abs.twimg.com/x-web/assets/og/default-og.a2e144f0cf66.jpg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://twitter.com/VeeIsForVampire/status/1764623237244170421\" target=\"_blank\"> Post </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://twitter.com/VeeIsForVampire/status/1764623237244170421\" target=\"_blank\"> https://twitter.com/VeeIsForVampire/status/1764623237244170421 </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> This post is from a protected account. </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://twitter.com/dork_tales/status/1764377806467953134\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://pbs.twimg.com/media/GHxUN-kagAA7U_j?format=webp&amp;name=large\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://twitter.com/dork_tales/status/1764377806467953134\" target=\"_blank\"> Dork Tales (from the dorkest timeline) (@dork_tales) on X </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://twitter.com/dork_tales/status/1764377806467953134\" target=\"_blank\"> https://twitter.com/dork_tales/status/1764377806467953134 </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> Let's turn the page. Here are some more pics from my anonymous friend about #curseborne </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-05T09:53:13-08:00","id":1532045,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/curseborne/1512116-curseborne?p=1531606#post1531606\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Awkward GM Corbin</b> is cracking everything we know about <b>Curseborne</b>! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/eek.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"EEK!\" smilieid=\"9\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=QzIw1R38RKY\" data-code=\"QzIw1R38RKY\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/QzIw1R38RKY/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div></div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you for the share, also check this new one about the mechanics and world elements we were introduced to:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://youtu.be/DhdmVCg-km0?si=OpqJ0A5XP4-R1FaU\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://youtu.be/DhdmVCg-km0?si=OpqJ0A5XP4-R1FaU\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://youtu.be/DhdmVCg-km0?si=OpqJ0A5XP4-R1FaU\" target=\"_blank\"> https://youtu.be/DhdmVCg-km0?si=OpqJ0A5XP4-R1FaU </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25291-donteatrawhagis","name":"DontEatRawHagis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"211"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-07T02:27:18-08:00","id":1532143,"title":"","content":"So do anyone have an idea on what Curseborne is?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","name":"MrornX","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"418"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-07T22:20:00-08:00","id":1532231,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrornX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/curseborne/1512116-curseborne?p=1532143#post1532143\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So do anyone have an idea on what Curseborne is?</div> </div> </div> </div>Currently, what we know is that in Curseborne player characters are the Accursed. There's a lot of different kinds of Accursed - the Hungry, which seem analogous to various kinds of undead including vampires and ghouls, Primals, which appear to be shapeshifters with an intimate connection to violence, struggle and primal elemental forces, and Outcasts, people who seem to occupy a liminal space in reality and society, among others. There are various social groups and subgroups within the categories we know, for instance Primals include Lykans/the Get of Lyka, which appear to have some connection to wolves and werewolf myths, and Raptors, which seem more related to primeval predators. <br /> <br /> &quot;Messing around&quot; with magic can end with you being Accursed, as can family inheritances. The various kinds of Accursed consider themselves part of an extended family, with subtypes being closer &quot;relatives&quot; and they seem to have a variety of shady connections, family holdings and shady connections which they politick over while maintaining the delicate balance between the needs of the different groups (the often ambitious Hungry clashing with the prickly and prone-to-violence Primals, for instance), while also dealing with some kind of liminal spaces/otherworlds known as the Outside and Battlegrounds, which seem to be a source of more inhuman monsters as well as being connected to the Curse which marks the Accursed. The big themes appear to be horror, mystery, and found family.<br /> <br /> What isn't known explicitly but can be speculated from the tone of what we can see is it's a modern horror game using the Storypath system that focuses on diverse &quot;families&quot; of people affected by supernatural phenomena, their lives, politics and struggles, probably with a humanist perspective drawn from modern horror (I personally detect bits that feel like they're drawing heavily on modern creepypasta style stories for the horror elements, though I haven't seen clear confirmation.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7},{"type":"\ud83d\ude00","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/364-logos-invictus","name":"Logos Invictus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-11T04:17:19-07:00","id":1532364,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Logos Invictus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/curseborne/1512116-curseborne?p=1532231#post1532231\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Currently, what we know is that in Curseborne player characters are the Accursed. There's a lot of different kinds of Accursed - the Hungry, which seem analogous to various kinds of undead including vampires and ghouls, Primals, which appear to be shapeshifters with an intimate connection to violence, struggle and primal elemental forces, and Outcasts, people who seem to occupy a liminal space in reality and society, among others. There are various social groups and subgroups within the categories we know, for instance Primals include Lykans/the Get of Lyka, which appear to have some connection to wolves and werewolf myths, and Raptors, which seem more related to primeval predators.<br /> <br /> &quot;Messing around&quot; with magic can end with you being Accursed, as can family inheritances. The various kinds of Accursed consider themselves part of an extended family, with subtypes being closer &quot;relatives&quot; and they seem to have a variety of shady connections, family holdings and shady connections which they politick over while maintaining the delicate balance between the needs of the different groups (the often ambitious Hungry clashing with the prickly and prone-to-violence Primals, for instance), while also dealing with some kind of liminal spaces/otherworlds known as the Outside and Battlegrounds, which seem to be a source of more inhuman monsters as well as being connected to the Curse which marks the Accursed. The big themes appear to be horror, mystery, and found family.<br /> <br /> What isn't known explicitly but can be speculated from the tone of what we can see is it's a modern horror game using the Storypath system that focuses on diverse &quot;families&quot; of people affected by supernatural phenomena, their lives, politics and struggles, probably with a humanist perspective drawn from modern horror (I personally detect bits that feel like they're drawing heavily on modern creepypasta style stories for the horror elements, though I haven't seen clear confirmation.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Interesting...<br /> <br /> Thanks for writing up all the info! I'll have to keep an eye on this..<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/\" target=\"_blank\">MrGone's Character Sheets</a><br /> For all your WoD Character Sheet Needs<br /> _________________________________<br /> Buy books &amp; pdfs from DTRPG and support my web site! <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=55414\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a><br /> Support my site on Patreon! <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mrgone\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","name":"Mr Gone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-11T11:22:58-07:00","id":1532384,"title":"","content":"Did anyone else find the e-mail link on the curseborne website? I mailed it and it said I was subscribed but I am curious if there have been other posts to the subscribers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11720-redwulfe","name":"Redwulfe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11720_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"570"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-20T14:38:08-07:00","id":1532919,"title":"","content":"Pure speculation on my part:<br /> <br /> I'm suspecting that the Accursed are kind of like the Exalted: in the same way Exalted has Solar Exalted, Lunar Exalted, Sidereal Exalted, Dragon-Blooded Exalted, and so on, each of which can be viewed <i>almost</i> but not quite as separate gamelines, so too Curseborne has Hungry Accursed, Primal Accursed, Outcast Accursed, etc. There are likely direct parallels between the different types of Accursed and the more popular gamelines in Chronicles of Darkness; so if you want something like the experience of playing Vampire: the Requiem, you can get it by focusing your Chronicle on Hungry Accursed; and if you want something like the experience of playing Werewolf: the Forsaken, you can get it by focusing your Chronicle on Primal Accursed.<br /> <br /> That said, the (e.g.) Primal Accursed are probably no more like the Uratha of WtF than the Garou of WtA or the Lunars of Exalted are. They'll be their own thing. I suspect that this will be especially true of whichever kind of Accursed ends up being the counterpart to mages: given that they're Accursed, I suspect there's going to be much more of a downside to them than you get in the Mage gamelines \u2014 perhaps something along the lines of Faustian Sorcery from CoD's Mage Chronicler's Guide, or the different Sources of Power for sorcerers in Scion's \u201cSaints and Monsters\u201d supplement.<br /> <br /> And unlike how CoD started with a default that each supernatural character type is a gameline unto itself, Curseborne appears to be using something more like the Exalted (or perhaps Contagion Chronicles) model, where the default assumption is that the various types of Accursed all interact with each other. So more integrated overall.<br /> <br /> I'm also hoping they implement something like the Myth Levels from Scion's \u201cMysteries of the World\u201d, where the Storyguide is given some \u201cdials and switches\u201d that he can use to tune the style of game that he intends to run, with one of those \u201cdials\u201d being how hidden or out in the open the supernatural is \u2014 ranging from \u201cmonsters lurk in the shadows, and the average mortal either doesn't know or at least pretends not to know that they're there\u201d to \u201cthe Accursed are out in the open and fully engaged in all aspects of mortal society\u201d. HtV-style Tiers would be another such dial. And so on.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":".  Typo 03-21-2024, 06:32 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-06T07:13:31-07:00","id":1533697,"title":"","content":"#Curseborn We have a small teaser from the upcoming book. This is a brief description and discussion of the antagonist - who is VERY reminiscent of the Trader from Goblin Market - or the True Fae from Changeling. \ud83d\ude31 From 45:10 Pathcast there is a description of Swap-Man. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/eek.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"EEK!\" smilieid=\"9\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/episode/6cEZZedgfMid7d4OUod4Ly\" target=\"_blank\">https://open.spotify.com/episode/6cEZZedgfMid7d4OUod4Ly</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 04-06-2024, 10:20 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-21T01:00:43-07:00","id":1536044,"title":"","content":"In less than a month, on <b>Onyx Path Con</b>, we should get first real Actual Play and 'World Premiere' of the game. Also, there will be <b>Curseborne Panel</b>! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> ( First is ar 6:00 PM on Friday 14th June - second is on 12:30 PM on Sunday 15th )<br /> <br /> <img data-align=\"none\" data-size=\"full\" loading=\"lazy\" border=\"0\" src=\"https://theonyxpath.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/05/Schedules_5_OP-791x1024.jpg\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"https://theonyxpath.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/05/Schedules_5_OP-791x1024.jpg\" data-thumb-url=\"https://theonyxpath.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/05/Schedules_5_OP-791x1024.jpg\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"\" class=\"bbcode-attachment thumbnail js-lightbox bbcode-attachment--lightbox\" itemprop=\"image\"/>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-23T08:55:00-07:00","id":1536156,"title":"","content":"<b>Awkward GM Corbin</b> got his hands on <b>#Curseborne</b> - the 'spiritual successor' to Chronicles of Darkness / the new World of Darkness from Onyx Path, using their d10 mechanics! \ud83d\ude32 Corbin looks through what went to sellers - and the game has a 'world premiere' at Onyx Path Con on June 15th - and the game is scheduled to go on sale in October 2024! \ud83d\ude31 Corbin presented many interesting facts and information in the material. <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=k-4XwVcolnE\" target=\"_blank\"> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=k-4XwVcolnE\" data-code=\"k-4XwVcolnE\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/k-4XwVcolnE/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div></a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 05-23-2024, 11:58 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-27T21:54:08-07:00","id":1536403,"title":"","content":"<b>Curseborne</b> brochure on that <b>Awkward GM Corbin</b> did video is now open to public, for free. \ud83d\ude0e <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/474861/curseborne-rpg-teaser\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/prod...rne-rpg-teaser</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-02T19:51:11-07:00","id":1536729,"title":"","content":"Well for anyone who was hoping that this would somehow not be as dark as either Chronicles or World (while still somehow being an urban horror setting in which you are the monster? I think was brought up once?), Curseborne seems...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Curseborne Preview PDF</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Curseborne is...<br /> <br /> \u2026the reason BAD THINGS happen to good people.<br /> \u2026being a MONSTER because that\u2019s what YOU DESERVE.<br /> \u2026being a MONSTER because some other FUCKER DESERVED IT and you\u2019re caught in the blast radius.<br /> \u2026resolving to be better, and failing miserably.</div> </div> </div> </div>...not really interested in that.<br /> <br /> Don't get me wrong, some of these lines definitely work that way, like...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Samesies</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u2026why we have to be ourselves, even when a SELFISH ASSHOLE wants to be us.<br /> \u2026redefining family, because the family, you can\u2019t choose PROBABLY SUCKS.\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>-and the sample art definitely hits the gothic tragic tradition as being alive and well, along with some of the 90s post neo-gothic vibes which taps more into ideas of redemption (thought notably with a color scheme that betrays that we're operating in an electroluminescent world rather than an incandescent one, which is an extremely nice touch), but honestly this feels a lot more punk than anything we've gotten in the urban horror scene, and not just because it feels more notably fatalistic, but also because it's... kind of just plain angrier? Just a lot more maligned about the whole thing?<br /> <br /> Like, we'll see how much that's the vibe, but it feels really contrasted against how, for however dark Chronicles was, it was a lot homier and generally hopeful in vibe. Like, yeah, it was dark, but it was primarily dark because it was a mysterious setting, and learning and unveiling was a major part of the entire thing, and for just as many terrible things as you could find, there was still room for the wonderous, the beautiful, the fascinating. Like, yes, the world of Chronicles was in a lot of ways fucked and you definitely wanted to work to make it better, but it was also a world where you could revel in every kind of wonderful between a hot dog and the vastness of the world in the Anima Mundi or the Shadow, where the human will could be felt in the Cave or in a fairy creature reaching across the chasm to hold your hand. Like, even if the world is kind of unfair and and broken, some of that is just how the game plays, and a certain peace not only has to be made with the cosmic horror, but <i>can</i> be made.<br /> <br /> Appropriate for a setting where it seems like everything may be borne from a malediction against something/everything else, Curseborne seems interested in selling a world where <i>blame</i> is the <i>appropriate response</i>, where even if it is the world, then the world should probably be made to burn. It's got an anger that feels most resonant, to me at least, with Deviant. It seems just seething with fury.<br /> <br /> And hey, we'll see if that's actually the case-heaven knows that read actually fits well with what I wanted from OP's take on the &quot;-of Darkness&quot; games (along with break the splat based divide and rebuilding along the social divides and leaning into more uniformity with modern horror), so I'm probably projecting a lot on it, but that's definitely a take I can see, nevermind get behind.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-03T19:32:16-07:00","id":1536778,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/curseborne/1512116-curseborne?p=1536729#post1536729\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well for anyone who was hoping that this would somehow not be as dark as either Chronicles or World (while still somehow being an urban horror setting in which you are the monster? I think was brought up once?), Curseborne seems...<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> ...not really interested in that.<br /> <br /> Don't get me wrong, some of these lines definitely work that way, like...<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> -and the sample art definitely hits the gothic tragic tradition as being alive and well, along with some of the 90s post neo-gothic vibes which taps more into ideas of redemption (thought notably with a color scheme that betrays that we're operating in an electroluminescent world rather than an incandescent one, which is an extremely nice touch), but honestly this feels a lot more punk than anything we've gotten in the urban horror scene, and not just because it feels more notably fatalistic, but also because it's... kind of just plain angrier? Just a lot more maligned about the whole thing?<br /> <br /> Like, we'll see how much that's the vibe, but it feels really contrasted against how, for however dark Chronicles was, it was a lot homier and generally hopeful in vibe. Like, yeah, it was dark, but it was primarily dark because it was a mysterious setting, and learning and unveiling was a major part of the entire thing, and for just as many terrible things as you could find, there was still room for the wonderous, the beautiful, the fascinating. Like, yes, the world of Chronicles was in a lot of ways fucked and you definitely wanted to work to make it better, but it was also a world where you could revel in every kind of wonderful between a hot dog and the vastness of the world in the Anima Mundi or the Shadow, where the human will could be felt in the Cave or in a fairy creature reaching across the chasm to hold your hand. Like, even if the world is kind of unfair and and broken, some of that is just how the game plays, and a certain peace not only has to be made with the cosmic horror, but <i>can</i> be made.<br /> <br /> Appropriate for a setting where it seems like everything may be borne from a malediction against something/everything else, Curseborne seems interested in selling a world where <i>blame</i> is the <i>appropriate response</i>, where even if it is the world, then the world should probably be made to burn. It's got an anger that feels most resonant, to me at least, with Deviant. It seems just seething with fury.<br /> <br /> And hey, we'll see if that's actually the case-heaven knows that read actually fits well with what I wanted from OP's take on the &quot;-of Darkness&quot; games (along with break the splat based divide and rebuilding along the social divides and leaning into more uniformity with modern horror), so I'm probably projecting a lot on it, but that's definitely a take I can see, nevermind get behind.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Honestly, having seen the character creation vids? I suspect that it's not that dark - it wants to be stark and neo-gothic, but there's nuance that can't be seen in a pamphlet. Like, for example, magic is <i>really cool, </i>so it's easy to see why Sorcerers get addicted to it. It's more Turbo-Awakening to be a Sorcerer than anything else.<br /> <br /> If anything, it gives a bottom to how far your characters can fall, and it's way, way above &quot;cannot climb out&quot; - Damnation is an always-lurking menace, but that's because &quot;losing all Curse Dice (mana that makes you more competent the more you have)&quot; is easy to do if you're desperate or not careful - and easily solved, simply regain a Curse Die. The theme of Damnation is &quot;Exalted Limit Break/having a really bad day and it's hard not to make that everyone else's problem&quot; not &quot;Humanity 0/you've become a monster to monsters.&quot; So, the unspoken part of &quot;failing miserably&quot; is &quot;so you try to redeem yourself again.&quot;<br /> <br /> And the Families...well, Black Hearts (Hungry - vampires) are outright Forever Knight-style Superheroes With Fangs, and proud of it (they rejected how amoral other Hungry are and chose to feed on emotion instead while trying to help others stay out of the Hungry's political games), Unburdened (Sorcerers) are socialist urban monks who actively try to help make the world better and shifted their entire magical style to help them do so, and Mavens (Dead - body-hopping ghosts) are professional party animals glad to have come back. We don't know a lot of Primals (werebeasts) in detail yet, but Hydes would very happily claim they deserve to be monsters - they worked <i>hard </i>on that superhuman serum to turn themselves into the Hulk, so they are going to very much show up at the next monster mash to be the strongman act (which makes them a lot closer to the actual Dr. Jekyll then most adaptations).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-03T20:38:15-07:00","id":1536780,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/curseborne/1512116-curseborne?p=1536778#post1536778\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Honestly, having seen the character creation vids? I suspect that it's not that dark - it wants to be stark and neo-gothic, but there's nuance that can't be seen in a pamphlet. Like, for example, magic is <i>really cool, </i>so it's easy to see why Sorcerers get addicted to it. It's more Turbo-Awakening to be a Sorcerer than anything else.<br /> <br /> If anything, it gives a bottom to how far your characters can fall, and it's way, way above &quot;cannot climb out&quot; - Damnation is an always-lurking menace, but that's because &quot;losing all Curse Dice (mana that makes you more competent the more you have)&quot; is easy to do if you're desperate or not careful - and easily solved, simply regain a Curse Die. The theme of Damnation is &quot;Exalted Limit Break/having a really bad day and it's hard not to make that everyone else's problem&quot; not &quot;Humanity 0/you've become a monster to monsters.&quot; So, the unspoken part of &quot;failing miserably&quot; is &quot;so you try to redeem yourself again.&quot;<br /> <br /> And the Families...well, Black Hearts (Hungry - vampires) are outright Forever Knight-style Superheroes With Fangs, and proud of it (they rejected how amoral other Hungry are and chose to feed on emotion instead while trying to help others stay out of the Hungry's political games), Unburdened (Sorcerers) are socialist urban monks who actively try to help make the world better and shifted their entire magical style to help them do so, and Mavens (Dead - body-hopping ghosts) are professional party animals glad to have come back. We don't know a lot of Primals (werebeasts) in detail yet, but Hydes would very happily claim they deserve to be monsters - they worked <i>hard </i>on that superhuman serum to turn themselves into the Hulk, so they are going to very much show up at the next monster mash to be the strongman act (which makes them a lot closer to the actual Dr. Jekyll then most adaptations).</div> </div> </div> </div>Admittedly I haven't checked those vids out. I'll need to.<br /> <br /> Gotta say, while I like OP's games, I don't often feel drawn to talk about them, and I was kind of leaning away from the forums. Curseborne feels like it won't have that problem, and that's nice.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-04T14:20:39-07:00","id":1536810,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/curseborne/1512116-curseborne?p=1536780#post1536780\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Admittedly I haven't checked those vids out. I'll need to.<br /> <br /> Gotta say, while I like OP's games, I don't often feel drawn to talk about them, and I was kind of leaning away from the forums. Curseborne feels like it won't have that problem, and that's nice.</div> </div> </div> </div>really happy to ready that Kelly","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-11T01:23:41-07:00","id":1537195,"title":"","content":"In latest Onyx Path News vlog Matthew is saying that <b>Spawn of Vodnik</b> from <b>Curseborne</b> is only genetic family of Primals. All others are chosen/not-blood related. ( At 8:50 of video ) <br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=UsjNv-Li3ck\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=UsjNv-Li3ck\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=UsjNv-Li3ck\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=UsjNv-Li3ck </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-11T05:01:15-07:00","id":1537201,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Character Creation info complied from Old Ways podcast about Curseborne </span><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"> \u2013</span><ul><li><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">There are <b><i>Linages</i></b> \u2013 general groupings od monsters you play as. There are 5 in game \u2013 <b>Outcast</b>,<b> Sorcerer</b>, <b>Hungry</b>,<b> Dead</b> and <b>Primal</b>. In the podcast all players made characters from <b><i>Outsiders</i></b> \u2013 mythical beings from <i>\u2018Heaven, Hell and all between, outside of Mundane World\u2019. </i>Outsiders, when loosing all Curse dices, drop their \u2018mask\u2019 and all can see they are those alien beings from other dimension. Mortals forget the event later, but to restore their connections, Outsiders then need to make new friends ( or deepen Bond with previous one ).</span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Each Linage has also <b><i>Torment</i></b>\u2013 they are Momentum gains. You pick one of two Torments listed per Linage \u2013 and then personal Trigger to those. </span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><b><i>Family</i></b>\u2013 your closest Family on Earth \u2013 they are like factions. <b>Battleground Angles</b> ( banished to the Earth, wanting to go for Battlegrounds ), <b>Chimera</b> ( tried to become gods ), <b>Nephilim</b> ( travellers through Outsides ), <b>Keepers of the Broken Vine</b> ( they are trapped on Earth and try to make it better ), </span><b><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Magnificent</span></b><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">( They try to redeem themselves to leave for Outside \u2013 granting wishes to other people ), <b>League of the Hidden Crossroads</b> ( Tempting people and being the person they need at crossroads )</span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><b><i>Linage</i></b> and<b><i> Family </i></b>are two separated Paths? <span style=\"font-family:Segoe UI Emoji\">\ud83e\udd14</span> <b><i>Role</i></b> is the Path of your \u2018everyday life\u2019, how you get money, what are you for general mortal population.</span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><b><i>Curse Dice Pool </i></b><b>\u2013 Start on 1, max 5. </b>It rises by one with each Entanglement. Any action you make ( you test ), you build your EVERY dicepool you test on Curse \u2013 and then add other dices from normal dicepool, to fill it up. Until you have Curse, you can use most magic. Without Curse, you lose most of magic.</span></li> </ul>EDIT: <b>AwkwardGM</b> has corrected me on Curse Dice - Specifically because when you run out of Curse Dice you essentially <b>&quot;Go Loud&quot;</b>:<ul><li>Primals - Go wild form and must attack things.</li> <li>Sorcerers - Must cast magic until they are able to sacrifice something to regain Curse dice.</li> <li>Outcasts - Lose all bonds and enrapture Mortals, until they make a meaningful bond with a mortal.</li> <li>Dead - Can't cast magic and are forced cause the emotion they are resonant to.</li> <li>Hungry - Can't cast magic and are forced to feed.\u200b</li> </ul><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=klEXpgXs3DQ&amp;t\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"font-family:Segoe UI\"> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=klEXpgXs3DQ&amp;t\" data-code=\"klEXpgXs3DQ\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/klEXpgXs3DQ/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div></span></a></span>\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 06-12-2024, 05:19 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-13T09:03:24-07:00","id":1537306,"title":"","content":"I admit I am interested in a vampire substitute and OPP is the only cure.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-13T12:33:23-07:00","id":1537315,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/curseborne/1512116-curseborne?p=1537306#post1537306\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I admit I am interested in a vampire substitute and OPP is the only cure.</div> </div> </div> </div>That goes to <b>Curseborne</b> analysis more - <b>Don't Vampire makes Hungry AND Dead at the same time in Linage model?</b> Can we then have MIXED Linage monsters?! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/eek.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"EEK!\" smilieid=\"9\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-13T19:54:31-07:00","id":1537326,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/curseborne/1512116-curseborne?p=1537315#post1537315\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That goes to <b>Curseborne</b> analysis more - <b>Don't Vampire makes Hungry AND Dead at the same time in Linage model?</b> Can we then have MIXED Linage monsters?! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/eek.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"EEK!\" smilieid=\"9\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>I'm confused at the concept of a vampire who can't cast magic!<br /> <br /> That would prevent me from being a Tremere...err Scholomance student!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-14T03:57:43-07:00","id":1537335,"title":"","content":"I suspect that the default assumption is going to be that if the monster you want to make potentially fits multiple Lineages, you have to pick one. So if you're looking at making an Outcast Primal Hungry Dead Sorcerer, you have to decide which one of those matters most.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-14T14:42:23-07:00","id":1537360,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/484466/curseborne-ashcan\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/prod...seborne-ashcan</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-15T00:39:39-07:00","id":1537383,"title":"","content":"(Double post)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 06-15-2024, 03:42 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-15T00:42:35-07:00","id":1537384,"title":"","content":"Like <b>Nicolas</b> pointed - <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/484466/curseborne-ashcan\" target=\"_blank\">Curseborne Ashcan is live on DriveThru!</a> Also, crowdfunding for whole book should be in October 2024. \ud83d\ude0e<br /> <br /> <img width=\"672\" height=\"960\" data-align=\"none\" data-size=\"full\" loading=\"lazy\" border=\"0\" src=\"https://d1vzi28wh99zvq.cloudfront.net/images/4261/484466.jpg\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"https://d1vzi28wh99zvq.cloudfront.net/images/4261/484466.jpg\" data-thumb-url=\"https://d1vzi28wh99zvq.cloudfront.net/images/4261/484466.jpg\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"\" class=\"bbcode-attachment thumbnail js-lightbox bbcode-attachment--lightbox\" itemprop=\"image\"/><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Reading <b><i>Linages</i></b> in Ashcan, here are short summary of Linages and their traits. I compare them to CoD various monsters splats, as they are closest to them \u2013 but still, Curseborne <i><b>Linages</b></i> are much more \u2018general\u2019 and \u2018archetypical\u2019. So here we go:</span><ul><li><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><b>Dead</b> \u2013 Revenants and Sin-Eaters \u2013 You died but stayed in your body. You now can leave the body as ghost, but you risking becoming not self-aware phantasm.</span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><b>Hungry</b> \u2013 Vampires and Beasts \u2013 You died but become insatiable undead being. You choose your Feeding type of blood, emotions or spirit essence and stick to it. You also gains Undead Strength powers, but those generate Bane for the scene \u2013 sunlight, silver or fire are just examples for those. You can gain more Strengths for gaining next Banes.</span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><b>Outcasts</b> \u2013 Part demons, angels, fae and a like \u2013 You have \u2018unhumane form\u2019 that is \u2018masked\u2019 most of the time and some supernatural feel about you. Can \u2018slip the Mask\u2019 and give a bit of you otherworld nature to mark social interaction with outers. Can go to the Battlegrounds, mixed half alien dimensions, half our Earth. When loosing Curse, you need to reconnect with humans \u2013 or being shunned out by any interactions with mortals.</span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><b>Primal </b>\u2013 Werewolves and other shapeshifters \u2013 You change into Wild Form, animal based Creature, always larger than human. Shapes of common animals, require specific spells. In all forms you have supernatural senses. Without Curse Dice, they transform into Wild Form and Creature need to be satisfied by it\u2019s instinctual behavior.</span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><b>Sorcerer </b>\u2013 Mages, sorcerers and witches \u2013 You are sorcerer with variety of spells at your disposal, but your magic is also somehow cursed. But we do not have any real mechanical info about them in Ashcan. <span style=\"font-family:Segoe UI Emoji\">\u2639</span> ( Waiting for crowdfunding for whole book info on it. ) </span></li> </ul><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">We also get 4 Ready Made characters for those Linages ( beside Sorcerers ).</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><b>Wyrd\u2019s Opinion:</b> I generally like this \u2018changes to genre\u2019 between CoD and Curseborne. <span style=\"font-family:Segoe UI Emoji\">\ud83d\ude0a</span> Only I\u2019m not sure I like that Primals need to burn extra spells slots to have other animal forms, compare to CoD Uratha what have all 5 forms from start. <span style=\"font-family:Segoe UI Emoji\">\u2639 </span></span>And we don't know anything about Sorcerers mechanics. <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Segoe UI Emoji\">\u2639</span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 06-15-2024, 11:51 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-15T06:23:55-07:00","id":1537393,"title":"","content":"I guess we have a few answers abou the mixed lineage thing now that we know Accursed can have spells of different lineages, to a certain degree.<br /> <br /> I am really curious now about sorcerers, that are probably the ones with less basic rules and most intense practice and spells interaction, afterall they are humans with magic capacities.<br /> <br /> I really love the way the many splats interact and can learn powers from eachother. Also the number of different monsters covered by each lineage, and the way the different families impact the character is really interesting (while we haven't see any kind of family references in the Ashcan)<br /> <br /> I have a few questions:<br /> - If the Hungry dont use their undead strength they can go around in the sun? I mean, the undead strength lasts for a scene and the banes are caused by them, so... no power no bane?<br /> - Why so much focus on angels and demons when Changelings are such a better reference for Outcasts?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-15T07:21:33-07:00","id":1537394,"title":"","content":"I'm working at the time that the Curseborne panel happens; so I'll have to catch up after the fact. Are these panels being posted on YouTube?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-15T07:30:42-07:00","id":1537395,"title":"","content":"They will all be on YouTube eventually, but they're on the Twitch channel from the moment they're recorded, so if you subscribe you can access all of them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#000080\">Matthew Dawkins</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000080\">In-House Developer for Onyx Path Publishing</span></b><br /> <br /> <i><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b><span style=\"color:#008080\">Website: </span><a href=\"http://www.matthewdawkins.com\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.matthewdawkins.com</span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#008080\">Patreon: </span><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins</span></a></b></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/152-the-gentleman-gamer","name":"The Gentleman Gamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar152_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-15T10:54:13-07:00","id":1537409,"title":"","content":"It feels far more like 2nd Edition WOD meets Chronicles of Darkness with all of the original things that OPP brought to the line and more versus another line's &quot;we demand to be taken seriously because we are ANGSTY and SERIOUS.&quot; Which is to say it's not so utterly wrapped up in its own misery and sorrow that it forgot that games are supposed to be <i>fun</i>.<br /> <br /> Basically, it takes a similar premise, &quot;We are monsters in a world of them&quot; and goes somewhere different with it.<br /> <br /> I am sold.<br /> <br /> I am glad OPP's creativity is on full display here and kind of now wonder if it would have been better to have done this from the beginning a decade ago. This could well be the Pathfinder we always needed.<br /> <br /> (and to clarify, I don't think this is remotely &quot;OPP'S World of Darkness&quot; but scratches the itch in a wholly original way that is uniquely theres)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 06-15-2024, 01:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-15T11:56:43-07:00","id":1537418,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">My Notes from <b>Curseborne Panel</b> on OPP Con 2024</span> <span style=\"font-family:Segoe UI Emoji\">\ud83d\ude0e</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Crowdfunding for <b>Curseborne</b> corebook -&gt; <b>October 1<sup>st</sup> 2024 </b>( for KS ending around Halloween</span> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"> <span style=\"font-family:Segoe UI Emoji\">\ud83d\ude0e</span></span>\u200b <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">)</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><b>What is Curseborn? -</b>&gt; \u2018Spiritual Successors\u2019 to WoD and CoD, as Onyx Path own IP.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><b>Curseborne</b> is mix of Urban Horror and some Punk and Hopepunk understones.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><b>Curseborne is start of very large line </b>- Gameline assumptions for now \u2013 You play low level Family member with low Entaglemnet. ( 1-5 ) Second book for \u2018Ancient Monsters\u2019 ( 6-10 ), with more Entaglemntes around your Family and Curse. Ideas for Player\u2019s Guide and fictions. \u2018Cursed World\u2019 locations book, around world, with important NPCs/SGCs. New Linages and Families book(s?).</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><b>Is there be metaplot or Lore?</b> There will be events, locations and NPCs mentioned. ( But no sWoD like \u2018metaplot\u2019 of \u2018and now Betharits are not playable\u2019. )</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><b>Magic system is similar to <i>\u2018At the Gates\u2019</i> mechanics.</b> <span style=\"font-family:Segoe UI Emoji\">\ud83d\ude0a</span>Linages have unique magics \u2013 but you can learn other Linages powers. So as Hungry you have Hungry spells \u2013 but can learn Primals shapeshifts. And Primals are not only animal spells \u2013 but also elemental.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><b>Will there be Slasher-like beings?</b> There will be creepypasta-like beings, probably new Linage.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><b>Every Family have internal conflict</b> \u2013 and that that are always some jerks and problematic parts in them. They are all very \u2018Found Family\u2019 concept.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><b>What\u2019s with a Moths symbols?</b> Active at night, undergone transformation from webs \u2013 and creature of darkness seeking light, that also easily die. Symbol as graffiti at the wall in setting.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><b>The \u2018I did a supernatural deal\u2019 ideas for characters?</b> Most would be that your ancestors made deal and you now need to live with the Curse, after sins of your ancestor.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><b>Everyone is using spells and Practices</b> \u2013 it takes from universal root of Curse, \u2018at the center of the world\u2019. You can pull up by the threads of Curse, to use your magic.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><b>Inspiration media</b> \u2013 <i><b>\u2018House of Usher\u2019</b></i> 2023 TV series, Urban Horror on general, <b>\u2018Unsolved Mysteries\u2019</b> Podcast</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><b>No AI art</b> \u2013 fresh artistist, not from WoD &amp; CoD already doing.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Daniel L. was <b>CurseBoi </b>on Discord <span style=\"font-family:Segoe UI Emoji\">\ud83d\ude09</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><b>Curseborne </b>ARG marketing campaign was having the biggest resposnes of every OPP game made EVER.</span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude0e","count":2},{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-15T12:12:14-07:00","id":1537425,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/curseborne/1512116-curseborne?p=1537409#post1537409\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am glad OPP's creativity is on full display here and kind of now wonder if it would have been better to have done this from the beginning a decade ago. This could well be the Pathfinder we always needed.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mm. From what they've said at the Con, it's been in active development for five years, a few years after Paradox bought the WW properties. Looking back, that seems about the time they would have known the writing was on the wall for Chronicles and they got to work on something of their own. I'm doubtful it could have been much earlier - circa Time of Judgment, WW were understandably attached to the WoD, knew their fandom was too, and didn't know how far they could break with it for the nWOD, only learning over time. And when OPP first formed there was no obvious reason to do a third dark urban fantasy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-15T18:57:54-07:00","id":1537447,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/curseborne/1512116-curseborne?p=1537409#post1537409\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It feels far more like 2nd Edition WOD meets Chronicles of Darkness with all of the original things that OPP brought to the line and more versus another line's &quot;we demand to be taken seriously because we are ANGSTY and SERIOUS.&quot; Which is to say it's not so utterly wrapped up in its own misery and sorrow that it forgot that games are supposed to be <i>fun</i>.<br /> <br /> Basically, it takes a similar premise, &quot;We are monsters in a world of them&quot; and goes somewhere different with it.<br /> <br /> I am sold.<br /> <br /> I am glad OPP's creativity is on full display here and kind of now wonder if it would have been better to have done this from the beginning a decade ago. This could well be the Pathfinder we always needed.<br /> <br /> (and to clarify, I don't think this is remotely &quot;OPP'S World of Darkness&quot; but scratches the itch in a wholly original way that is uniquely theres)</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree with you and can't stress enough that the writing is clear that it takes itself seriously, but doesn't feels desperate for you to do so. Like, it's a pretty dark game setting so far(I distinctly feel like I will have to do a lot less reminding that this is, in fact, an urban horror game), but you get the feeling that, if the game were a person (and the GM), it'd just shrug if someone said &quot;My character is Lucky from Lucky Charms as makes sense in this world&quot; and roll with it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude0e","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-15T22:01:13-07:00","id":1537461,"title":"","content":"Finished the Ashcan.<br /> <br /> Just for my money, in the line up with it's spiritual predeccesors, Curseborne still reads as being somehow the bleakest of the three settings-but also the punkiest, and that punk energy of taking all this shit that's been done to you and to the world and doing what you will with it(which can include kicking against the pricks, though I'm not sold on this idea of hopepunk* in the game from the Ashcan) is definitely a heady fucking drug**. I'm not quite sold on Storypath Ultra as the foundation for it's mechanics-I'm gonna need to chew on the execution for a bit-but for the vibes alone, I'm down for it. This is some sharp, fierce shit, and I like it.<br /> <br /> *Which isn't a particular problem for me, since I still find hopepunk to be something of an oxymoronic label and so far unsuccessful in holding my attention when invoked, so.<br /> **though, as I mentioned, one thing I think will work for a lot of people is that's not insistent on that bleakness or punkiness-you can definitely see a lot of room to tell a lot of stories the way they'll want to. In fact, while I will stick to this as my read, I'm not going to be surprised if a lot of people don't get that vibe at all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-16T04:38:52-07:00","id":1537479,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/curseborne/1512116-curseborne?p=1537461#post1537461\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Finished the Ashcan.<br /> <br /> Just for my money, in the line up with it's spiritual predeccesors, Curseborne still reads as being somehow the bleakest of the three settings-but also the punkiest, and that punk energy of taking all this shit that's been done to you and to the world and doing what you will with it(which can include kicking against the pricks, though I'm not sold on this idea of hopepunk* in the game from the Ashcan) is definitely a heady fucking drug**. I'm not quite sold on Storypath Ultra as the foundation for it's mechanics-I'm gonna need to chew on the execution for a bit-but for the vibes alone, I'm down for it. This is some sharp, fierce shit, and I like it.<br /> <br /> *Which isn't a particular problem for me, since I still find hopepunk to be something of an oxymoronic label and so far unsuccessful in holding my attention when invoked, so.<br /> **though, as I mentioned, one thing I think will work for a lot of people is that's not insistent on that bleakness or punkiness-you can definitely see a lot of room to tell a lot of stories the way they'll want to. In fact, while I will stick to this as my read, I'm not going to be surprised if a lot of people don't get that vibe at all.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, what I really like is how blase the in-character writing is about the downsides of being cursed; Claudia outright says nobody's responsible for the existence of curses, they're occult entropy, and leads with a disclaimer on how difficult Damnation is with &quot;you may think magic is cool because...it is&quot;. The theme clearly isn't desperate to sell you on angst, the fact your powers are dependent on something called a Damnation works enough.<br /> <br /> This makes it a way better read than a lot of the more self-serious WoD stuff; one gets the sense that the average Sorcerer would talk to a Hollow One or Nephandus about philosophy and quickly start fighting the urge to start wanking the air - &quot;life's hard, water's wet, all sad, we get it, up the fuck shut.&quot; Which is not a bad thing at all; like how Cassie ends her discussion on how every Outcast myth of their glorious otherwordly homeland is a comforting lie with &quot;we can use that as an ideal to achieve, not a past to mourn.&quot; It's an absolute refusal to let themselves be broken by the world, and that's an attitude that makes the grim nature of curses way more palatable.<br /> <br /> Does make me fear for the world if a Reeve met a Chakravanti, precisely becaue they wouldn't air wank. More like get along like the house they set on fire.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-16T06:25:15-07:00","id":1537481,"title":"","content":"Do we get any info on antagonist groups, full monsters, mortal interference, and similar &quot;opposing force&quot; factions?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/543-professor-phobos","name":"Professor Phobos","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-16T06:56:18-07:00","id":1537484,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Professor Phobos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/curseborne/1512116-curseborne?p=1537481#post1537481\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do we get any info on antagonist groups, full monsters, mortal interference, and similar &quot;opposing force&quot; factions?</div> </div> </div> </div>We actually get a good look at how weird the non-Accursed monsters are; there's only three fully statted, but beyond the basic flesh-eating zombie, who is actually pretty hardy, we have Drones, who are proof of how scary the malevolent supernatural can be (they're mortals that have had any ability to feel or connect eaten out of them, turning them into meek, helpless shells of themselves - a really distinct scene in the quickstart is meeting two non-hostile Drones, and it's clear they literally can't muster up the will to clean themselves under their own power), and Shattered Spaces, which are haunted areas. Not monsters in the area, the area themselves; while the Outside happily seeps into everywhere it can and creates Liminalities, anomalies in space and time that can be any sort of noun, most of those are only incidentally dangerous, even interstitial zones (sentient pockets in reality that want to be lived in - so they make themselves inviting and secure so you don't want to leave as badly). Shattered Spaces are what happens when it's an utterly malevolent part of the Outside coming through, making the area alive, sentient, and hungry. As well as a beachhead for whatever hell spawned them, sooner or later. See: Silent Hill (though Silent Hill itself may be a Battleground, a portion of the Outside that burrowed into the mortal world, that opens to traumatized people).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-16T22:13:25-07:00","id":1537545,"title":"","content":"My review I put on DriveThru on Ashcan...<br /> <br /> <b>4/5 Stars</b><br /> <br /> <b>Curseborne Ashcan is not perfect. I\u2019m not saying is bad\u2026</b><br /> I\u2019m old WoD and CoD Storyteller. I was at the start ( and even few years before ) of coming of New World of Darkness in 2004 and stick to all the line of CoD for all it\u2019s run till 2020, supporting almost all gamelines. I\u2019m also Storypath veteran, running 3 gamelines of it to this day.<br /> <br /> And I must say that Curseborne Ashcan is not perfect. I\u2019m not saying is bad \u2013 only it leaves me in few places too much to wondering about game. In the end, I\u2019m waiting for crowdfunding manuscript of whole book coming in October 2024.<br /> <br /> Pros:<ul><li>Interesting and \u2018dynamic\u2019 changes to previous concepts in WoD and CoD.</li> <li>Interesting model and mechanics of using Curse dices</li> <li>Refreshing look on genere by Linages and their new takes on old monster archetypes.</li> <li>Return to Urban Horror setting after those 4-5 years. \ud83d\ude0a</li> </ul><br /> Cons:<ul><li>Ashcan don\u2019t show \u2018bigger picture\u2019. I still literally don\u2019t know how should I run the game or how general world/setting of game looks from characters point of view.</li> <li>Somehow illogical position of Families in 3 Paths system \u2013 Families are dependent on Linages already, being subPath locked itself, not free option choosing like in different Storypaths.</li> <li>No real mechanics and descriptions what are Sorcerers in the setting.</li> <li>A bit too much vulgar language to my taste in in-person descriptions.</li> </ul>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 06-17-2024, 01:16 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-17T10:41:42-07:00","id":1537566,"title":"","content":"Does anyone have a link or connection to the Sorcerer Creation Vid?<br /> <br /> I have found the others, but this one is eluding me. It is no longer up on Rolling Nomad's Twitch or YouTube channels. I do have the crib sheet someone made, but I would like to watch the video if possible.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11720-redwulfe","name":"Redwulfe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11720_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"570"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-13T02:21:53-07:00","id":1538510,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://www.podbean.com/ep/pb-eybr9-1666dcc\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Onyx Pathcast Episode with answers on Curseborne</b></a>! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><ul><li>Curse dice</li> <li>Liminal spaces</li> <li>Sorcerers?</li> <li>Primals vs. Hungry</li> <li>Entanglement</li> <li>Aspirations</li> <li>Primal shifting</li> <li>Teamwork</li> <li>Stacking</li> <li>World book</li> <li>Metaplot and Lore</li> <li>Ages</li> <li>Sorcerers</li> <li>Foes</li> <li>Ashcan PoD</li> <li>Foundation spells</li> </ul>So I like how Sorcerers are 'addicted to magic' and they have 'eating disorder on casting magic'. When they lose all Curse Dice, they NEED to cast magic, until they Sacrifice things they Family point to. They WANTED to have magic so much - they are Cursed all they time, on they own wanting. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/eek.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"EEK!\" smilieid=\"9\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 07-13-2024, 07:15 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}